/**
 * Festivals of Sikkim.
 *
 * The Government of Sikkim publishes its own account of twenty-two
 * observances, naming the community each belongs to. That page is the spine of
 * this category, because community attribution is exactly the thing travel
 * writing gets wrong — a Limbu festival described as "Buddhist", a Rai
 * festival folded into "Nepali". Where the state names a community, so do we.
 *
 * Dates that follow the Tibetan lunar calendar move every year. Each story
 * gives the lunar position and the usual Gregorian window, and none of them
 * invents a date for a specific year.
 */

